<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Esztergom</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Gran</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Esztergom is a city in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a> on the right bank of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/danube">Danube</a>, facing Štúrovo in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slovakia">Slovakia</a>. It was the seat of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arpad">Árpád</a> grand princes and the first royal capital of Hungary, traditionally the birthplace of Stephen I, and from about 1000 the see of the archbishop and primate of Hungary. Its 19th-century basilica is the largest church in the country.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/esztergom.jpg" alt="Esztergom" width="320" height="428" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: see above · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:EsztergomMontage2.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
